    "Both engines completed all 60 primary lifecycle checks, including a 131,070-token prompt with two generated tokens, four concurrent requests, and replay after cancellation.",
    "The extensible candidate committed 5.15 GiB after warmup. Its full-attention pool gained 63 usable 128-token blocks, increasing capacity from 159,104 to 167,168 tokens. Mamba and sliding-window capacities stayed constant.",
    "Single-request median decode rose 8.2% to 9.8% at 512 to 4,097 tokens across the measured workloads. At 16,384 tokens, single-request decode rose 0.3% cold and 1.2% warm. Four-request cold chat was the largest decline, with 1.5% lower per-request decode and 1.8% lower wave throughput.",
    "All 48 aligned and unaligned cold responses matched the baseline token for token, as did the corresponding warm responses. For 1,024-token chat, 5 of 15 cold comparisons matched and 0 of 15 warm comparisons matched. Within each version, all 15 cold/warm chat pairs diverged at median token index 17.",
    "The candidate skipped synthetic mixed warmup because that batch requested 21 Mamba blocks from a pool of 17 physical blocks. The real mixed lifecycle passed all 16 checks, including concurrent decode and external RAM restoration."
